       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum is 10 mg per day, and 50 mg once daily is five times that. An overdose at that level can cause profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. The risk is higher because amlodipine's half-life is long (30 to 50 hours).\n\nIf 50 mg was a typo, I can enter one of these instead:\n- **5 mg orally once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg orally once daily.** This is the maximum dose.\n\nIf you meant something else, such as a different drug or a different total dose, tell me and I'll adjust. If the patient has already received a dose this large, that's an overdose. It needs urgent clinical assessment and a call to poison control or toxicology.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
